 # Epipolar Sampling
-
-
 ## Overview
-Epipolar sampling is a class of techniques that place sample points along epipolar lines to exploit geometric smoothness and reduce computation. In participating media rendering, it places samples along rays emanating radially from a light source's projection on the screen to exploit the smooth variation of inscattered light along these lines [S2, unofficial]. In multi-view neural rendering, it samples features from other views along epipolar lines corresponding to a given ray, enabling cross-view feature aggregation without full 3D volume rendering [S1, unofficial]. Both variants reduce the number of expensive ray-marching or feature-interpolation steps compared to uniform sampling [S2, unofficial][S1, unofficial].
